cerberus-api for Debian
=======================

The service is installed but NOT enabled or started (it needs site config and an
AWS Nitro-enabled EC2 host running the cerberus-signer enclave). To bring it up:

  1. Create the config from the example and lock it down:
       cp /usr/share/cerberus/config.yaml.example /etc/cerberus/config.yaml
       chown root:cerberus /etc/cerberus/config.yaml
       chmod 0640 /etc/cerberus/config.yaml
  2. Install the Kerberos keytab referenced by keytab_path (mode 0600 or 0400).
  3. Review /etc/default/cerberus-api (AWS_REGION, CONFIG_PATH, ...).
  4. Enable and start:
       systemctl enable --now cerberus-api

The cerberus system user and /var/log/cerberus are created automatically via
systemd-sysusers / systemd-tmpfiles on install. See RUNBOOK.md in this directory.

 -- Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>
